      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a very difficult and lonely feeling when a diagnosis feels like a description of a permanent state rather than a treatable condition. The loss of a sense of self and purpose often feels more like a quiet death than a medical issue, leaving you with no one to blame and no way \"out.\" Please remember that you don't have to explain the \"nothingness\" alone, and even if hope feels distant, a safe space to just sit with these feelings is always more available than you know.",
